  "body": "What happens: the post-merge gate run 43671481030 on `085a4717e` fails at the step `clippy -D warnings` on the Linux runner.\n\nEvidence:\n\n```\nerror: constant `PNG_256` is never used\n  --> crates/ui/src/egui_app/app_icon.rs:12:7\nerror: function `taskbar_icon` is never used\n  --> crates/ui/src/egui_app/app_icon.rs:40:8\nerror: could not compile `camcraft-ui` (lib) due to 2 previous errors\n```\n\nCause: PR 1764 added the Windows taskbar icon. The caller is behind `cfg(windows)`. The constant and the function are not. On Linux and macOS they are dead code.\n\nExpected: clippy with `-D warnings` is clean on Windows, Linux and macOS.\n\nDone means: `PNG_256` and `taskbar_icon` (and any item only they use) compile only where they are used, or are used on every OS. Clippy for `camcraft-ui` is clean. The Windows behaviour does not change.\n",
